      "match_notes": "<p>Opening&nbsp;pair&nbsp;Crawley&nbsp;(106)&nbsp;&amp;&nbsp;D.&nbsp;Beaver&nbsp;100&nbsp;Not&nbsp;Out&nbsp;put&nbsp;on&nbsp;196&nbsp;for&nbsp;1st&nbsp;wkt.&nbsp;It&nbsp;was&nbsp;Crawley&#39;s&nbsp;powerful&nbsp;hitting&nbsp;of&nbsp;7&nbsp;Sixes&nbsp;&amp;&nbsp;5&nbsp;Fours&nbsp;whereas&nbsp;in&nbsp;comparison&nbsp;D.&nbsp;Beaver&nbsp;only&nbsp;hit&nbsp;13&nbsp;fours&nbsp;to&nbsp;push&nbsp;the&nbsp;Visitors&nbsp;to&nbsp;declare&nbsp;on&nbsp;229/2.&nbsp;Only&nbsp;4&nbsp;extras&nbsp;were&nbsp;conceded&nbsp;by&nbsp;Rainhill&nbsp;in&nbsp;which&nbsp;our&nbsp;Overseas&nbsp;Pro&nbsp;Imli&nbsp;Lemtur&nbsp;bowled&nbsp;21.3&nbsp;overs&nbsp;to&nbsp;take&nbsp;2&nbsp;for&nbsp;82.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>In&nbsp;reply&nbsp;Rainhill&nbsp;made&nbsp;more&nbsp;cautious&nbsp;progress&nbsp;with&nbsp;Captain&nbsp;Ben&nbsp;Edmundson&nbsp;compiling&nbsp;the&nbsp;top&nbsp;score&nbsp;of&nbsp;59&nbsp;which&nbsp;included&nbsp;7&nbsp;Fours.&nbsp;Openers&nbsp;Forsyth&nbsp;21&nbsp;&amp;&nbsp;McGladdery&nbsp;30&nbsp;put&nbsp;on&nbsp;on&nbsp;52&nbsp;for&nbsp;the&nbsp;1st&nbsp;wkt.&nbsp;It&#39;s&nbsp;good&nbsp;to&nbsp;see&nbsp;the&nbsp;tail&nbsp;end&nbsp;making&nbsp;a&nbsp;good&nbsp;contribution&nbsp;with&nbsp;Jack&nbsp;Lowrie&nbsp;hitting&nbsp;22&nbsp;including&nbsp;3&nbsp;Fours&nbsp;only&nbsp;to&nbsp;be&nbsp;Stumped&nbsp;and&nbsp;stalled&nbsp;at&nbsp;162&nbsp;All&nbsp;Out.&nbsp;Rainhill&nbsp;4&nbsp;pts,&nbsp;Wallasey&nbsp;25&nbsp;pts.</p>\r\n",
